# 7. Docker Image Was Not Updated

### Problem

I changed Python, HTML, or CSS files, but the browser still showed the old version.

### Root Cause

The running container may still be using the old Docker image.

### Fix

Rebuild the application:

```bash
docker compose up -d --build
```

The `--build` option tells Docker to rebuild the image before starting the container.

### Without `--build`

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

This normally starts the existing image.

### With `--build`

```bash
docker compose up -d --build
```

This rebuilds the image and then starts the containers.

